  {
   "id": 517581,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Isabelle’s gross income is $93,450. She paid $7,840 in mortgage interest and $3,810 in property taxes. She also donated $1,500 to her favorite charity. What is Isabelle’s AGI?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Add the deductions: 7,840 + 3,810 + 1,500 = $13,150.</p>\n<p>Subtract the legal deductions from the gross income to find the adjustable gross income (AGI).</p>\n<p>93,450 – 31,150 = $80,300</p>\n<p>The AGI is $80,300.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$80,300"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
